---
import WritingLayout from '../../layouts/WritingLayout.astro';
import ChloeArchitecture from '../../components/ChloeArchitecture.astro';
const decisions = [
  { title: 'Hybrid retrieval for institutional content', text: 'Weaviate combines Titan Text Embeddings v2 with BM25 to match both natural-language questions and exact program names. The knowledge base is the primary source; retrieval quality depends on the coverage and freshness of its content.' },
  { title: 'A limited fallback to official sources', text: 'The agent can use Exa on FSU domains when the knowledge base is insufficient. Each question allows two knowledge-base searches and one web search, limiting external calls while preserving a path to information outside the index.' },
  { title: 'Serverless hosting with progressive responses', text: 'FastAPI runs on AWS Lambda arm64 through the Lambda Web Adapter and a streaming Function URL. NDJSON events show the draft as it is generated; a final event replaces it with the checked answer and sources. The tradeoffs are startup overhead and draft text that may change after validation.' },
];
---
<WritingLayout title="Chloe: a RAG assistant for CCI, FSU">
  <article>
    <p class="kicker">Solution architecture case study</p>
    <p class="lead">I built an assistant that helps visitors find information about Florida State University’s College of Communication &amp; Information. The system connects content ingestion, retrieval, and a streaming chat interface, with explicit controls over sources and model usage.</p>
    <dl class="project-facts">
      <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Ingestion → retrieval → chat</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Core stack</dt><dd>FastAPI · Bedrock · Weaviate · AWS Lambda</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <section aria-labelledby="problem-title">
      <h2 id="problem-title">The problem</h2>
      <p>CCI spans three schools, with admissions, programs, and deadlines that vary by school and student level. A useful assistant needs to clarify that context, retrieve relevant institutional content, and give visitors sources they can verify.</p>
      <p>I designed around four requirements: institutional content first, clarification before guessing, bounded model and search usage, and a response the interface can display progressively.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="solution-title">
      <h2 id="solution-title">The solution</h2>
      <p>An ingestion pipeline prepares content for Weaviate. At query time, FastAPI validates the request and verifies Cloudflare Turnstile before invoking a pydantic-ai agent powered by Claude Haiku 4.5 on Amazon Bedrock.</p>
      <p>The agent clarifies ambiguous questions, declines unrelated requests, and retrieves supporting content before answering factual questions. The backend removes sources that did not come from a search. If no valid source remains, it returns a no-information response.</p>
    </section>

    <ChloeArchitecture />

    <section aria-labelledby="decisions-title">
      <h2 id="decisions-title">Architecture decisions</h2>
      <div class="decisions">{decisions.map(decision => <div class="decision"><h3>{decision.title}</h3><p>{decision.text}</p></div>)}</div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="controls-title">
      <h2 id="controls-title">Trust boundaries and operating limits</h2>
      <p>Browser-supplied history is untrusted: only the last six turns are passed as quoted context. Each question is capped at <strong>five tool calls</strong>, <strong>eight model requests</strong>, <strong>800 output tokens</strong>, and a <strong>60-second</strong> Lambda execution window.</p>
      <p>Turnstile and request limits constrain access and usage. They do not replace traffic-level rate limits or spending controls. Source checking establishes provenance; it does not prove that every claim is supported or fully prevent prompt injection.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="operations-title">
      <h2 id="operations-title">Deployment and observability</h2>
      <p>Terraform provisions the Lambda, streaming endpoint, permissions, logs, and S3 artifact storage. Secrets load from encrypted Systems Manager parameters at startup. CloudWatch captures application logs; Langfuse records model calls, tool calls, and token usage through OpenTelemetry.</p>
      <p>The service depends on Bedrock access, available secrets, and a populated Weaviate collection. These dependencies, along with external search, need monitoring alongside the API.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="demonstration-title">
      <h2 id="demonstration-title">Leadership Board demonstration</h2>
      <p>I presented the assistant at a CCI Leadership Board meeting at Florida State University. Attendees tried it live with questions about the college, alongside off-topic and playful prompts. In those interactions, the assistant stayed within its intended scope.</p>
      <p>The session provided direct feedback from stakeholders and an opportunity to observe the assistant outside prepared examples.</p>
      <a class="recap-link" href="https://lnkd.in/p/eJTJ_A8f" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the presentation recap ↗</a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="outcome-title">
      <h2 id="outcome-title">Outcome and next validation</h2>
      <p>The implementation connects the ingestion pipeline to a source-linked chat experience, with explicit paths for clarification, off-topic questions, and missing information.</p>
      <p>The current estimated cost is <strong>about $0.01 per question-and-answer exchange</strong>.</p>
      <p>Answer quality, latency, and adoption have not been quantified here. The next step is an evaluation set across all three schools to test retrieval relevance, citation support, and no-information behavior, followed by latency and concurrency testing.</p>
    </section>
    <a class="closing-link" href="/#projects">← Explore other projects</a>
  </article>
</WritingLayout>
<style>
  article { margin-top:24px; }
  .kicker { color:var(--orange);font:12px/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .lead { max-width:66ch;font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,21px);line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:20px 0 32px; }
  .project-facts { display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr;gap:24px;margin:0;padding:20px 0;border-block:1px solid var(--line); }
  dt { font:11px/1.6 var(--font-mono);color:var(--orange);margin-bottom:6px; }
  dd { margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6; }
  section { margin-block:48px;max-width:72ch; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 18px; }
  section > h2::after { content:'';display:block;width:72px;height:2px;background:var(--orange);margin-top:14px; }
  h3 { font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:0 0 10px; }
  p { color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;line-height:1.8; }
  .decision + .decision { margin-top:24px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
  .decision p { margin-bottom:0; }
  strong { color:var(--ink);font-weight:500;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--orange) 55%,transparent);text-underline-offset:4px;text-decoration-thickness:1px; }
  section[aria-labelledby="outcome-title"] { padding:24px;border-left:2px solid var(--orange);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--orange) 4%,var(--bg)); }
  section[aria-labelledby="outcome-title"] > h2::after { display:none; }
  section[aria-labelledby="outcome-title"] p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }
  .recap-link { display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--orange);text-underline-offset:5px;transition:color 160ms; }
  .recap-link:hover { color:var(--orange); }
  .closing-link { display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:var(--muted);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);transition:color 160ms; }
  .closing-link:hover { color:var(--ink); }
  @media(max-width:639px) { .project-facts { grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px; }section { margin-block:36px; } }
</style>
